@CoreWeave launched Forge on September 30, 2026 at its Fully Connected conference — a development layer that runs the full AI loop of train, observe, curate, improve, and evaluate in one connected environment open across models, frameworks, and clouds, the Nasdaq-listed AI cloud said in its press release.

Forge unifies Weights & Biases Models, OpenPipe post-training expertise, and open-source marimo notebooks with CoreWeave services. Shipping pieces include generally available ARIA (coding agent over experiment and observability data), Agent Lens for production-agent traces, generally available Sandboxes, Registry for versioned checkpoints, serverless RL and supervised fine-tuning, plus Free, Pro, and Enterprise editions. MasterClass and Canva are already building on Forge, CoreWeave said.

Why it matters: named public Big Tech/cloud CoreWeave platform launch with dated company primary — irreversible product FACT unused this week. Sources: CoreWeave, 30 Sep 2026.

